From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwe666 <64239822+qwe3017@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: dts: hg5585f: enable the WED/WDMA blocks

Enables the WED instances and the WDMA block described by
an7581-wed.dtsi on the FiberHome HG5585F (the common dtsi, so both the
CT and the CU variant get it).

This follows the stock H3C HM2004-DU, which is a two-radio design:
its 14c3:790a part is driven through npu_offload_mapping while its
14c3:7906 part is in whnat's support list, i.e. driven through WED.
mt_whnat is loaded there and its IRQ fires (773 interrupts in eight
seconds), so WED is not a dead path -- it is the one the vendor ships.

This board has a single MT7916D (the 7906 one), hence WED.

The nodes already carry airoha,wed-ops and airoha,attach-enable, so
status = "okay" is all that is needed; without it airoha-wed keeps
doing its dry run (program the hardware, then roll back).

---
 target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-fiberhome-hg5585f-common.dtsi | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

--- a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-fiberhome-hg5585f-common.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-fiberhome-hg5585f-common.dtsi
@@ -381,3 +381,31 @@
 	phys = <&usb1_phy PHY_TYPE_USB2>;
 	vusb33-supply = <&reg_usb_3p3v>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Wi-Fi downlink offload: bring up the two WED instances and the WDMA block.
+ *
+ * The board's MT7916D enumerates through two PCIe HIFs (PCIe1 primary,
+ * PCIe0 secondary), which is why the SoC exposes two WED instances.
+ *
+ * This is the stock H3C configuration. HM2004-DU is a two-radio design --
+ *   lspci 01:00.0 14c3:790a  ->  npu_offload_mapping  (NPU path)
+ *   lspci 01:00.0 14c3:7906  ->  whnat_cap_support()  (WED path)
+ * and this board carries a single MT7916D, i.e. the 7906 one, so WED is the
+ * route the vendor actually ships for it.
+ *
+ * The nodes already carry airoha,wed-ops / airoha,attach-enable, so "okay"
+ * is all that is needed -- the driver attaches for real instead of doing its
+ * dry run. Both registers where our old value disagreed with the stock device
+ * (WED_PCIE_INT_CTRL POLL, WED_WDMA_RX_THRES_CFG) now default to the stock
+ * values; the module parameters / DT properties pcie-poll-mode and
+ * rx-thres-mode switch back to the vendor-source values without a reflash.
+ */
+
+&wed {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&wdma {
+	status = "okay";
+};
